       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the maximum recommended metformin dose. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI suspect a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg** three times daily (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg**, or another dose in the standard range, such as 500 mg two or three times daily\n- **1000 mg** twice daily (2,000 mg/day)\n\nTell me the dose, and whether you want immediate-release or extended-release. I'll enter it right away with the note \"with meals.\" If 4250 mg really is what you intend, please confirm that explicitly and give me the clinical rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
